with the Christmas period well and truly  upon us it seems like a good time to  explore some of the weirdest Christmas  traditions around the world  [Music]  one of the most amusing traditions that  I've come across can be found in the  Catalan region of Spain and features  Theodore Nadal the Christmas log  sometimes referred to as the poop log  because of its poop like appearance I  guess the process begins when a branch  from the Yule tree is hollowed out and  the character is created complete with  legs smiley face and even a floppy red  hat the tradition begins on the 8th of  December when families bring out the  smile in log every night until Christmas  Eve the children are given the task of  feeding the log by filling it up with  nuts dried fruits and sweets once the  children are done they then cover the  log with a blanket to keep it warm on  Christmas Eve the families gather around  the log and proceed to beat the log of  sticks while they sing traditional songs  when the blanket is removed it appears  as if the log has pooped out a part of  sweets and presents for all of the  family once this process is complete the  poop log is then thrown into the fire  and the logs last Christmas gift is the  gift of warmth in Norway they believe  that Christmas Eve coincides of the  arrival of evil spirits and witches with  brooms being the preferred method of  transportation for most witches it seems  reasonable to hide all your brooms right  we can assume now that we're vacuum  cleaners being part of most households  the tradition of hiding your broom  sticks before you go to sleep may not be  as popular as it once was whilst on the  topic of evil spirits and mischievous  creatures we travel to Greece where the  callee cancellous make an appearance at  this time of year in many countries  around the world and in Greek folklore  the Kali cancerous are a race of  malevolent goblins that dwell  underground  on Christmas Day they make their way to  the surface where they remain for the 12  days of Christmas until January 6th when  they return to their home they often  described as small dark creatures who've  a long black tail their diet consists of  mainly small critters such as worms  snails and frogs their fear of the Sun  means that they only come out of hiding  during the evening and can be seen  climbing through windows and down  chimneys once inside a household they do  tend to cause havoc it became common for  families to place a colander on their  doorstep in order to keep them away  these goblins were believed to be rather  stupid and they could only count to two  meaning they would spend all night  counting the holes in the colander other  methods of protection involved placing  the black cross on your door and burning  the shoe as the smell will keep them  away overall they are not particularly  dangerous but they are mischievous and  rather troublesome  now when it comes to decorate in a  Christmas tree in Ukraine it's tradition  to use artificial spiders and webs  rather than tinsel and baubles the roots  of this tradition can be found in the  story of the spider in the Christmas  tree the story is about a family who  grew a pine tree for Christmas but  unfortunately they were too poor to  afford decorations  these spiders that lived in the family's  Hut heard the children crying before  they went to bed about how bad the  Christmas tree was and so the spiders  decided that they would create beautiful  silk webs to decorate the tree with when  the children are woke on Christmas  morning they were delighted with their  newly decorated tree and from that day  on the family never considered  themselves poor they were extremely  grateful of the gift they had been given  in Ukraine spiderwebs are believed to  give good fortune for the upcoming year  on the topic of strange decorations  there were some German families who  would hide a pickle in their Christmas  tree on Christmas Eve the first child to  discover it on Christmas Day  would be rewarded with a gift in South  Africa they do have some rather interest  in traditions when most people are  enjoying a traditional Christmas dinner  the locals prefer to tuck into some deep  fried caterpillars not exactly a meal  for those of you who are squeamish  children in South Africa told a chilling  story about a young boy named Danny on  Christmas Eve Danny's grandmother left  cookies out for Santa and once she had  gone to bed  Danny snuck downstairs and ate all of  the cookies when his grandmother found  out she was furious and in her rage she  killed Danny  he's ghost is said to haunt the homes of  misbehaving children around Christmas  the Krampus schlaf of the Krampus run is  something that we've discussed before  and takes place in Austria and several  other Bavarian countries adults dress up  as the demon Krampus and walk through  town scaring children almost like a  Halloween but where the roles are  reversed the adults are the ones now  dressing up and scaring the children  into behaving  in some parts of Italy they do not wait  for the arrival of Santa instead la  Befana often referred to as the good  which much like Santa Claus she hands  out gifts and presents to children  around Christmastime there are weird and  fun traditions all around the world and  if you know of any or even partake in  any traditions that I haven't mentioned  feel free to let me know in the comments  below as always I've been your host  mythology and fiction explained  [Music]  you
 

